 unfriendly and dont care attitue of admin staff", "text": "cleaner than lasdt year. great temple but lack of information on poojas opening hours. admin staff are not interested in selling /canvssing for poojas office opening hours do not align with temple opening hours.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "EE9B7E5DEAB98BF7FFFBA7EAAE3C5E90", "name": "thuraisingam52", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/thuraisingam52", "username": "thuraisingam52", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e5/2b/default-avatar-2020-52.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-06", "published_at_date": "2018-09-06"}, {"review_id": 614278093, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r614278093-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "cleaner than last year. poor service by admin staff. lack of information especially in english", "text": "when i visited at around 3:00 pm serprisingly not many people because main shrine was closed. finally we foundout it opens at 5;30pm. there was a price list for pooja at admin office but the staff were not interested in selling them. finally my Nepali friend got some information on the pooja details. went to book but was told no atm or electronic transfer facility except for donation. we went back with money at 5:30 pm when the temple opened. there were no staff at the office. they said the office closed at 4:pm so it appears no pooja in the evenings other than aarathi at the river. I could not understand the office hours. counters open when temple is closed and counter closed when temple open. it appears they discourage performing poojas. temple is cleaner this time than last year", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "EE9B7E5DEAB98BF7FFFBA7EAAE3C5E90", "name": "thuraisingam52", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/thuraisingam52", "username": "thuraisingam52", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e5/2b/default-avatar-2020-52.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-06", "published_at_date": "2018-09-06"}, {"review_id": 613724126, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r613724126-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Har Har Mahadev", "text": "You get great divine vibration. Please do not miss the evening aarti. Ensure you have sufficient time to go around the temple as the temple complex is very big.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D11321EC71AD75FFFC575E77289D6AB4", "name": "Narayanan Ganesan", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Ganesan4088", "username": "Ganesan4088", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/7e/22/e9/ganesan4088.jpg", "contribution_count": 149, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 15363680, "location_name": "Janakpuri", "location_name_detailed": "Janakpuri, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-04", "published_at_date": "2018-09-04"}, {"review_id": 613663100, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r613663100-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Pashupatinath Temple", "text": "Go to Temple after 09:30AM on a working day to avoid crowd. (Monday is holiday)\nYou will have  crowd on Holidays/festivals.\nDon't get caught up by guides or priests...\n\nMust see Bagmati river Aarti in evening.\nVery pleasant atmosphere with live singing.\nGo little early  to have right spot.\nIt is Free.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "BFB41C687C018C47BF443177B6F0268A", "name": "Pramod K", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/92pramodk", "username": "92pramodk", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0f/5a/a9/2a/pramod-k.jpg", "contribution_count": 9, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255060, "location_name": "Sydney", "location_name_detailed": "Sydney, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-04", "published_at_date": "2018-09-04"}, {"review_id": 613161776, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r613161776-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Wow! Unusual experience to see", "text": "We visited here knowing that only Hindu's are permitted to visit inside the temple, however our guide took us for a tour around the outside where able to watch several very public cremations taking place by the river side. I have never seen this before and felt a little uncomfortable / intrusive watching Nepali families saying goodbye to their loved ones in such a very public manner. We also saw several Holi men which are willing to pose with us for photos (obviously for a tip to do so). All in all a very different experience for us, glad we did it", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2F16305DB9F3451EBF935A7ACE7162DD", "name": "hellenback18", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/hellenback18", "username": "hellenback18", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/86/5c/d6/hellenback18.jpg", "contribution_count": 42, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-02", "published_at_date": "2018-09-02"}, {"review_id": 613139700, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r613139700-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Impressive and completely unexpected little Varanasi", "text": "Not far from Kathmandu you may find this little Varanasi complex with their gats, temples, crematory rituals, families...a place full of life...and death.\n\nWe felt a lot of respect and spent some time just watching the ceremonies and activities. You may be surprised but we took no photos...our family felt it was the wrong place to do so. \n\nAn absolutely must in Kathmandu, along with the Stupa and the morning flight to the Himalayas!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "91076EDF25C0601B98D1883D3DB36C59", "name": "Familia TM", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/familiaTM", "username": "familiaTM", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com